SUMMARY:Agent Con Raleigh 
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nWe are partnering with the Global AI All
 iance for their AgentCon event. If you are interested you must register on
  their website:\n\n[https://globalai.community/chapters/raleigh/events/age
 ntcon-raleigh/](https://globalai.community/chapters/raleigh/events/agentco
 n-raleigh/)\n\nJoin us for the AI Agents World Tour\, a global series of o
 ne-day conferences designed exclusively for developers building the future
  with AI agents.\n\nWhat to Expect:\n\n* Deep-Dive Talks from AI pioneers 
 and industry leaders\n* Technical Workshops on building\, deploying\, and 
 scaling agents\n* Live Demos of powerful open-source frameworks and tools\
 n* Networking with a global community of builders and innovators\n\nOur co
 nfounder\, [Mark Hinkle](https://www.linkedin.com/in/markrhinkle/)\, will 
 be conducting a session:\n\n### Get an Agent Running in 90 Minutes\n\nMay 
 6\, 10:20 a.m. - 11:50 a.m.\n\nI've sat through enough AI conference sessi
 ons where someone demos an agent doing something impressive and then says 
 "and you can do this too!" — and everyone goes back to their hotel room 
 and does nothing. This workshop is designed to fix that.\n\nIn 90 minutes\
 , we're going to get you actually running an AI agent. Not planning one. N
 ot white-boarding one. Running one. You'll leave with two tools in your to
 olkit that take completely different approaches to autonomous AI\, and you
 'll have hands-on time with both.\n\nWe'll dig into Manus\, one of the mos
 t capable multimodal agent platforms available right now. It handles text\
 , images\, and complex research tasks in a way that honestly still surpris
 es me. It's not cheap — the usage-based pricing adds up fast if you're n
 ot paying attention — but for the right use cases\, it earns its keep. W
 e'll run real tasks and talk through where the cost is justified and where
  it's going to burn a hole in your pocket.\n\nThen we'll flip to Claude Co
 work\, which takes a different approach entirely. It doesn't have Manus's 
 native image capabilities\, but if you're doing anything that involves bui
 lding or managing software — local file access\, coding projects\, autom
 ating workflows on your own machine — Cowork is genuinely impressive. We
 'll build something real with it during the session.\n\nThe point isn't to
  declare a winner. These tools solve different problems. The point is that
  by the end of this workshop\, you'll know which one to reach for and you'
 ll have actually used it\, not just watched someone else use it.
